  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Electricity Generation — ARIMA Forecasting\n","\n","Synthetic monthly series demonstrating a practical time-series workflow."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np,pandas as pd,matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from statsmodels.tsa.arima.model import ARIMA\n","from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error\n","rng=np.random.default_rng(42); dates=pd.date_range('2015-01-01','2024-12-01',freq='MS'); t=np.arange(len(dates))\n","s=pd.Series(12000+55*t+1100*np.sin(2*np.pi*t/12)+rng.normal(0,450,len(t)),index=dates)\n","train=s.iloc[:-12]; test=s.iloc[-12:]\n","fit=ARIMA(train,order=(1,1,1)).fit(); forecast=fit.forecast(12)\n","print('MAE:',mean_absolute_error(test,forecast))\n","plt.plot(train,label='Train');plt.plot(test,label='Actual');plt.plot(forecast,label='Forecast');plt.legend();plt.title('Electricity Generation Forecast')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Modelling caution\n","Compare multiple models and use rolling validation where appropriate. History length, seasonality and structural change materially affect forecasts."]}
 ],
